    </p><a href="/">← Home</a><pagefind-searchbox></pagefind-searchbox><script type="module" src="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.js"></script><script type="text/javascript" src="/static/pagefind.js"></script><h1 class="register-section" data-pagefind-body="1" data-pagefind-weight="10" data-pagefind-sort="title">AMEVTYPER1&lt;n&gt;_EL0, n = 0 - 15</h1><p class="insn_subtitle" data-pagefind-body="1">Activity Monitors Event Type Registers 1</p><div data-pagefind-body="1">
        <p>Provides information on the events that an auxiliary activity monitor event counter <a href="AArch64-amevcntr1n_el0.html">AMEVCNTR1&lt;n&gt;_EL0</a> counts.</p>
      </div><h3>Configuration</h3><p>AArch64 System register AMEVTYPER1&lt;n&gt;_EL0 bits [31:0] are architecturally mapped to AArch32 System register <a href="AArch32-amevtyper1n.html">AMEVTYPER1&lt;n&gt;[31:0]</a>.</p><p>AArch64 System register AMEVTYPER1&lt;n&gt;_EL0 bits [31:0] are architecturally mapped to External register <a href="amu.amevtyper1n.html">AMEVTYPER1&lt;n&gt;[31:0]</a>.</p><p>This register is present only when FEAT_AMUv1 is implemented and auxiliary activity monitor event counter &lt;n&gt; is implemented. Otherwise, direct accesses to AMEVTYPER1&lt;n&gt;_EL0 are <span class="arm-defined-word">UNDEFINED</span>.</p><h3>Attributes</h3>
        <p>AMEVTYPER1&lt;n&gt;_EL0 is a 64-bit register.</p>
      <h2>Field descriptions</h2><table class="regdiagram" id="fieldset_0"><thead><tr><td>63</td><td>62</td><td>61</td><td>60</td><td>59</td><td>58</td><td>57</td><td>56</td><td>55</td><td>54</td><td>53</td><td>52</td><td>51</td><td>50</td><td>49</td><td>48</td><td>47</td><td>46</td><td>45</td><td>44</td><td>43</td><td>42</td><td>41</td><td>40</td><td>39</td><td>38</td><td>37</td><td>36</td><td>35</td><td>34</td><td>33</td><td>32</td></tr></thead><tfoot><tr><td>31</td><td>30</td><td>29</td><td>28</td><td>27</td><td>26</td><td>25</td><td>24</td><td>23</td><td>22</td><td>21</td><td>20</td><td>19</td><td>18</td><td>17</td><td>16</td><td>15</td><td>14</td><td>13</td><td>12</td><td>11</td><td>10</td><td>9</td><td>8</td><td>7</td><td>6</td><td>5</td><td>4</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>0</td></tr></tfoot><tbody><tr class="firstrow"><td class="lr" colspan="32"><a href="#fieldset_0-63_16">RES0</a></td></tr><tr class="firstrow"><td class="lr" colspan="16"><a href="#fieldset_0-63_16">RES0</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="16"><a href="#fieldset_0-15_0">evtCount</a></td></tr></tbody></table><h4 id="fieldset_0-63_16">Bits [63:16]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Reserved, <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
    </div><h4 id="fieldset_0-15_0">evtCount, bits [15:0]:
      </h4><div class="field"><p>Event to count. The event number of the event that is counted by the auxiliary activity monitor event counter <a href="AArch64-amevcntr1n_el0.html">AMEVCNTR1&lt;n&gt;_EL0</a>.</p>
<p>It is <span class="arm-defined-word">IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED</span> what values are supported by each counter.</p>
<p>If software writes a value to this field which is not supported by the corresponding counter <a href="AArch64-amevcntr1n_el0.html">AMEVCNTR1&lt;n&gt;_EL0</a>, then:</p>
<ul>
<li>It is <span class="arm-defined-word">UNPREDICTABLE</span> which event will be counted.
</li><li>The value read back is <span class="arm-defined-word">UNKNOWN</span>.
</li></ul>
<p>The event counted by <a href="AArch64-amevcntr1n_el0.html">AMEVCNTR1&lt;n&gt;_EL0</a> might be fixed at implementation. In this case, the field is read-only and writes are <span class="arm-defined-word">UNDEFINED</span>.</p>
<p>If the corresponding counter <a href="AArch64-amevcntr1n_el0.html">AMEVCNTR1&lt;n&gt;_EL0</a> is enabled, writes to this register have <span class="arm-defined-word">UNPREDICTABLE</span> results.</p><p>The reset behavior of this field is:</p><ul><li>On a Warm reset, 
      this field resets
       to an architecturally <span class="arm-defined-word">UNKNOWN</span> value.</li></ul></div><div class="access_mechanisms"><h2>Access Instructions</h2>
        <p>If &lt;n&gt; is greater than or equal to <a href="AArch64-amcgcr_el0.html">AMCGCR_EL0</a>.CG1NC or <span class="xref">FEAT_AMUv1p1</span> is implemented and auxiliary counter &lt;n&gt; is not implemented, then reads and writes of AMEVTYPER1&lt;n&gt;_EL0 are <span class="arm-defined-word">UNDEFINED</span>.</p>
      <p>Accesses to this register use the following encodings in the System register encoding space:</p><div class="access_block"><div class="encoding"><p class="asm-code">MRS &lt;Xt&gt;, AMEVTYPER1&lt;n&gt;_EL0
          ; Where n = 0-15</p></div></div><p style="text-align: right">
      (op0 = 0b11, op1 = 0b011, CRn = 0b1101, CRm = 0b111:n[3], op2 = n[2:0])
      </p><p class="pseudocode">
let n:integer = UInt(CRm[0] :: op2[2:0]);

if !(IsFeatureImplemented(FEAT_AMUv1) &amp;&amp; IsG1ActivityMonitorImplemented(n)) then
    Undefined();
elsif n &gt;= NUM_AMU_CG1_MONITORS then
    Undefined();
elsif HaveEL(EL3) &amp;&amp; PSTATE.EL != EL3 &amp;&amp; EL3SDDUndefPriority() &amp;&amp; CPTR_EL3().TAM == '1' then
    Undefined();
elsif PSTATE.EL == EL0 then
    if AMUSERENR_EL0().EN == '0' then
        AArch64_SystemAccessTraptoEL1orEL2(0x18);
    elsif EL2Enabled() &amp;&amp; CPTR_EL2().TAM == '1' then
        AArch64_SystemAccessTrap(EL2, 0x18);
    elsif EL2Enabled() &amp;&amp; EffectivelyAtEL0NotInHost() &amp;&amp; IsFeatureImplemented(FEAT_FGT) &amp;&amp; (!HaveEL(EL3) || SCR_EL3().FGTEn == '1') &amp;&amp; HAFGRTR_EL2()[(2 * n) + 19] == '1' then
        AArch64_SystemAccessTrap(EL2, 0x18);
    elsif HaveEL(EL3) &amp;&amp; CPTR_EL3().TAM == '1' then
        if EL3SDDUndef() then
            Undefined();
        else
            AArch64_SystemAccessTrap(EL3, 0x18);
        end;
    else
        X{64}(t) = AMEVTYPER1_EL0(n);
    end;
elsif PSTATE.EL == EL1 then
    if EL2Enabled() &amp;&amp; CPTR_EL2().TAM == '1' then
        AArch64_SystemAccessTrap(EL2, 0x18);
    elsif EL2Enabled() &amp;&amp; IsFeatureImplemented(FEAT_FGT) &amp;&amp; (!HaveEL(EL3) || SCR_EL3().FGTEn == '1') &amp;&amp; HAFGRTR_EL2()[(2 * n) + 19] == '1' then
        AArch64_SystemAccessTrap(EL2, 0x18);
    elsif HaveEL(EL3) &amp;&amp; CPTR_EL3().TAM == '1' then
        if EL3SDDUndef() then
            Undefined();
        else
            AArch64_SystemAccessTrap(EL3, 0x18);
        end;
    else
        X{64}(t) = AMEVTYPER1_EL0(n);
    end;
elsif PSTATE.EL == EL2 then
    if HaveEL(EL3) &amp;&amp; CPTR_EL3().TAM == '1' then
        if EL3SDDUndef() then
            Undefined();
        else
            AArch64_SystemAccessTrap(EL3, 0x18);
        end;
    else
        X{64}(t) = AMEVTYPER1_EL0(n);
    end;
elsif PSTATE.EL == EL3 then
    X{64}(t) = AMEVTYPER1_EL0(n);
end;
                </p><div class="access_block"><div class="encoding"><p class="asm-code">MSR AMEVTYPER1&lt;n&gt;_EL0, &lt;Xt&gt;
          ; Where n = 0-15</p></div></div><p style="text-align: right">
      (op0 = 0b11, op1 = 0b011, CRn = 0b1101, CRm = 0b111:n[3], op2 = n[2:0])
      </p><p class="pseudocode">
let n:integer = UInt(CRm[0] :: op2[2:0]);

if !(IsFeatureImplemented(FEAT_AMUv1) &amp;&amp; IsG1ActivityMonitorImplemented(n)) then
    Undefined();
elsif n &gt;= NUM_AMU_CG1_MONITORS then
    Undefined();
elsif IsHighestEL(PSTATE.EL) &amp;&amp; !ImpDefBool("AMEVCNTR1_EL0()[n] is fixed") then
    AMEVTYPER1_EL0(n) = X{64}(t);
else
    Undefined();
end;
                </p></div><hr class="bottom_line"></hr><p class="copyconf">Version 2026.09 — Copyright © 2010-2026 Arm Limited or its affiliates.</p><small>This site is provided as a community resource and is NOT affiliated with nor endorsed by Arm Limited.</small><!-- Cloudflare Pages Analytics --><script defer src='https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js' data-cf-beacon='{"token": "de55e78a4e194365a81a0724c5c0ee91"}'></script><!-- Cloudflare Pages Analytics --></body></html>
